WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:05.624
This is Jarvis, an AI assistant I built that runs on my own computer.

2
00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:09.053
It opens apps, manages files, sets reminders,

3
00:00:09.053 --> 00:00:11.263
and remembers what I tell it.

4
00:00:12.167 --> 00:00:15.291
This is the real console, running on localhost.

5
00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:18.815
You bring your own key, and it stays on your machine.

6
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.606
Simple commands never wait for a model.

7
00:00:22.606 --> 00:00:27.225
The time, the date, or a change of screen is matched directly,

8
00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:29.684
so the answer comes back at once.

9
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.492
Here I type plain English to move between screens:

10
00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:37.683
the universe view, home, and my routines.

11
00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:41.808
Or I can just speak, after the wake word, hey Jarvis.

12
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:50.063
Under the hood, a Python FastAPI core streams events over WebSockets to an Electron desktop app,

13
00:00:50.063 --> 00:00:52.364
which starts the core for you.

14
00:00:52.364 --> 00:00:57.426
Voice uses Whisper, with voice activity detection and a wake word.

15
00:00:57.426 --> 00:01:00.724
It understands English, Tamil and Tanglish.

16
00:01:01.633 --> 00:01:04.036
Everything else goes to a model:

17
00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:08.315
Claude, Gemini, or a local model when the internet drops.

18
00:01:08.315 --> 00:01:12.220
It picks from a hundred and three tools, for memory,

19
00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:15.673
reminders, routines, files and a second brain.

20
00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.951
And it can't do damage by accident.

21
00:01:18.951 --> 00:01:21.677
Dangerous commands are blocked outright.

22
00:01:21.677 --> 00:01:23.994
Risky ones stop and ask, by click,

23
00:01:23.994 --> 00:01:26.787
by voice, or a thumbs down to the camera.

24
00:01:26.787 --> 00:01:28.423
Deletes go to the Trash.

25
00:01:29.333 --> 00:01:30.204
One real bug:

26
00:01:30.204 --> 00:01:33.353
the new desktop app connected to an old version

27
00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:36.032
that was still running on the same port.

28
00:01:36.032 --> 00:01:38.176
Now the core reports a build id,

29
00:01:38.176 --> 00:01:41.525
and the app only adopts a core from its own build.

30
00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:45.972
It has more than fifteen hundred automated tests,

31
00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.716
and the code is open source on GitHub.

32
00:01:48.716 --> 00:01:50.377
The link is on my site.

